18408219</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haag-Kerwer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Grams</surname><given-names>TEE</given-names></name><name><surname>Olivares</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Arndt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Popp</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Medina</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>L&#x000fc;ttge</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparative measurements of gas-exchange, acid accumulation and chlorophyll <italic>a</italic> fluorescence of different species of <italic>Clusia</italic> showing C<sub>3</sub> photosynthesis, or crassulacean acid metabolism, at the same field site in Venezuela</article-title><source>New Phytologist</source><year>1996</year><volume>134</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>226</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammel</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>New species of Clusiaceae from Central America with notes on synonomy in the tribe Clusieae</article-title><source>Selbyana</source><year>1986</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>112</fpage><lpage>120</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holtum</surname><given-names>JAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Aranda</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Virgo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gehrig</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>&#x003b4;<sup>13</sup>C values and crassulacean acid metabolism in <italic>Clusia</italic> species from Panama</article-title><source>Trees</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>658</fpage><lpage>668</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holtum</surname><given-names>JAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>JAC</given-names></name><name><surname>Neuhaus</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intracellular transport and pathways of carbon flow in plants with crassulacean acid metabolism</article-title><source>Functional Plant Biology</source><year>2005</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>429</fpage><lpage>449</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holtum</surname><given-names>JAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Degrees of crassulacean acid metabolism in tropical epiphytic and lithophytic ferns</article-title><source>Australian Journal of Plant Physiology</source><year>1999</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>749</fpage><lpage>757</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holtum</surname><given-names>JAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Weeks</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sexton</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Crassulacean acid metabolism in the ZZ plant</article-title><source>Zamioculcas zamiifolia <italic>(Araceae)</italic>. American Journal of Botany</source><year>2007</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>1670</fpage><lpage>1676</lpage></element-citat